Z||000000||costly86gt||05-09-2000||08:47 PM||||When I turn the steering wheel sometimes I hear this fast clicking noise.I hear it could be the cv joints.Is there anything it could be?||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||05-09-2000||10:18 PM||||It could be several things, but it's very unlikely it's CV joints. On a Fiero, they do not pivot like on a front wheel drive car. The CV joints on a Fiero are on the rear and are fixed into place. Does the noise sound like it's coming from inside the car, or outside front, or outside back?||||reg||1
Z||000002||costly86gt||05-10-2000||03:15 PM||||The noise sound like it is coming from the front of the car.It doesn't sound like it's on the inside.<p>[This message has been edited by costly86gt (edited 05-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fiasco||05-10-2000||11:37 PM||||Well, the easily checked things would be the clearance in the wheel well- is the tire rubbing on anything when you turn? Possibly something stuck in a tire?  If not, check & repack or maybe replace wheel bearings and check out the spindles for uneven wear or scoring. If it isn't any of this, turn up the radio so you can't hear it.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
